KEYBOARD WORKFLOW (R28) — scenario M of scripts/premium-ui-ux-probe.mjs
HEAD 7c3c2a2 · audit host, 2026-09-03 · against the real artifact behind the TLS front
$ node scripts/premium-ui-ux-probe.mjs --url https://172.20.10.2:3001 --only M [--auth]

The claim under test: a keyboard-only user can complete a whole tool workflow —
open the file dialog, run the tool, and act on the result — with no mouse event
dispatched at any point. Every activation below is recorded at the capture phase
by a listener installed before the first Tab, so "focus was on the control" and
"the control was activated" are separate observations.

The one seam, stated plainly: DOM.setFileInputFiles supplies the two files. The
OS file dialog is not driveable from any probe, so what M2 proves is that Enter
on the drop control fires the hidden input's own click() — the last thing the page
controls before the OS takes over. Choosing a file inside that dialog is not
exercised here and is not claimed.

